{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1537323-new-to-scarred-lands-some-questions","id":1537323,"title":"New to Scarred Lands... some questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scarred Lands"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-13T15:38:15-07:00","id":1537323,"title":"New to Scarred Lands... some questions","content":"Hi Folks,<br /> <br /> I picked up a d20-alternate system the other day (called MythCraft) and I was wondering what setting to use. I thought that maybe Scarred Lands might fit.<br /> <br /> But I had some questions before diving in:<br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>QUESTION 1 - Changes to the default setting</b><br /> <br /> For me, the Divine War taking place only 150 years ago seems too recent. It's something so incredibly mythic happening only a couple of generations ago to what seems like an established medieval society, and I ask myself: why didn't this war take place in the primeval dawn of the world? So\u2026 one idea was to push back the Divine War to, say, 10,000 years ago. If I did that, would it mess up a lot of the published material and create a lot of work for me?<br /> <br /> My second idea was to keep the time of the Divine War as it is - taking place 150 years ago - but instead of a medieval society, I would go with a Bronze Age society and really push a Greek Myth feel with epic heroes and gods larger than life, etc (maybe I could get Relics &amp; Rituals: Olympus for ideas). If I did that, and painted the Scarred Lands with a Bronze Age brush with mythic heroes, gods and monsters, would that mess with the published material and create a lot of work for me also?<br /> <br /> <b>QUESTION 2 - Lore in the Creature Collection and Relics &amp; Rituals books</b><br /> <br /> Because I won\u2019t be running 3E for the Scarred Lands, I\u2019m wondering whether I bother getting all of the Creature Collection and Relics &amp; Rituals books (and Divine &amp; the Defeated book). These books are cheap as chips to buy, but I would only be getting them for the lore, not the stat blocks. So, my question is: are these books worth getting just for the lore?<br /> <br /> (The books I\u2019ve decided to get so far are just: Ghelspad hardcover, Termana hardcover and Lost Tribes of the Scarred Lands hardcover. All of those cover the geographical regions of the Scarred Lands.)<br /> <br /> <b>QUESTION 3 - Order of reading</b><br /> <br /> If I do pick up all of the Creature Collection and Relics &amp; Rituals books (and Divine &amp; the Defeated) in addition to the 3 campaign books, what would be the best order to read them?<br /> <br /> Normally when a campaign setting comes out, the core book is released, and then monster and treasure and gods books follow. With Scarred Lands, the Creatures and Rituals books came out first (well, at least volume 1 of each). So would you read these books as they were released - ie. starting with the Creature Collection first? Or would you read the campaign setting books first - ie. starting with the Ghelspad hardcover?<br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28521-deceased","name":"deceased","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T20:21:50-07:00","id":1537328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deceased</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1537323-new-to-scarred-lands-some-questions#post1537323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Folks,<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>QUESTION 1 - Changes to the default setting</b><br /> <br /> For me, the Divine War taking place only 150 years ago seems too recent. It's something so incredibly mythic happening only a couple of generations ago to what seems like an established medieval society, and I ask myself: why didn't this war take place in the primeval dawn of the world? So\u2026 one idea was to push back the Divine War to, say, 10,000 years ago. If I did that, would it mess up a lot of the published material and create a lot of work for me?<br /> <br /> My second idea was to keep the time of the Divine War as it is - taking place 150 years ago - but instead of a medieval society, I would go with a Bronze Age society and really push a Greek Myth feel with epic heroes and gods larger than life, etc (maybe I could get Relics &amp; Rituals: Olympus for ideas). If I did that, and painted the Scarred Lands with a Bronze Age brush with mythic heroes, gods and monsters, would that mess with the published material and create a lot of work for me also?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the second option is much closer to the Scarred Lands as presented, and will require far less work. Your main concerns I'd imagine would be restricting weapons and armor technology (removing Steel, mostly). The setting leans heavily on the recency of the Divine War and the effects it has had on the landscape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deceased</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1537323-new-to-scarred-lands-some-questions#post1537323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>QUESTION 2 - Lore in the Creature Collection and Relics &amp; Rituals books</b><br /> <br /> Because I won\u2019t be running 3E for the Scarred Lands, I\u2019m wondering whether I bother getting all of the Creature Collection and Relics &amp; Rituals books (and Divine &amp; the Defeated book). These books are cheap as chips to buy, but I would only be getting them for the lore, not the stat blocks. So, my question is: are these books worth getting just for the lore?<br /> <br /> (The books I\u2019ve decided to get so far are just: Ghelspad hardcover, Termana hardcover and Lost Tribes of the Scarred Lands hardcover. All of those cover the geographical regions of the Scarred Lands.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Creature Collections, Relics and Rituals, and Divine and Defeated are dripping with setting material and lore. I think they do as much, if not more, to define the setting than the 3e location material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deceased</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1537323-new-to-scarred-lands-some-questions#post1537323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>QUESTION 3 - Order of reading</b><br /> <br /> If I do pick up all of the Creature Collection and Relics &amp; Rituals books (and Divine &amp; the Defeated) in addition to the 3 campaign books, what would be the best order to read them?<br /> <br /> Normally when a campaign setting comes out, the core book is released, and then monster and treasure and gods books follow. With Scarred Lands, the Creatures and Rituals books came out first (well, at least volume 1 of each). So would you read these books as they were released - ie. starting with the Creature Collection first? Or would you read the campaign setting books first - ie. starting with the Ghelspad hardcover?<br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> Thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that reading order is going to matter a whole lot. I'd probably start with Ghelspad and then go into the Divine and the Defeated, then bounce around from there, but I really think it's a matter of where you want to focus your attention first. I don't think there's much impact in the reading order.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T20:40:35-07:00","id":1537330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1537323-new-to-scarred-lands-some-questions?p=1537328#post1537328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the second option is much closer to the Scarred Lands as presented, and will require far less work. Your main concerns I'd imagine would be restricting weapons and armor technology (removing Steel, mostly). The setting leans heavily on the recency of the Divine War and the effects it has had on the landscape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Well, I'll read Ghelspad first. Maybe I'll be OK with it &quot;as is&quot; and won't need to make any changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1537323-new-to-scarred-lands-some-questions?p=1537328#post1537328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Creature Collections, Relics and Rituals, and Divine and Defeated are dripping with setting material and lore. I think they do as much, if not more, to define the setting than the 3e location material.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, great. I'll grab these, too. It's easy to find hard copies and they are still affordable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28521-deceased","name":"deceased","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T14:13:33-07:00","id":1542393,"title":"","content":"I know that this is an old thread, but I figure it's not that old so maybe you'll see it. <br /> <br /> The divine war having happened in living memory and heroes from the divine war still living among some of the races is a huge part of what makes Scarred Lands different from other settings. Changing it to have happened thousands of years ago would make it much more generic and much less unique. <br /> <br /> Also, Scarred Lands 3rd edition is far different from Scarred Lands PF / 5e. Many of the playable races in the latter are considered irredeemably evil in the previous edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}